  "id": "t1-coupling-v3",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In t1-coupling-v2 (readout-77681c90f98c8fd897882945), 14/16 Tier 1 tasks passed (including two_pole, model_vae_hard, interp_sparse_arc, mxfp8, and nvfp4), while ae_gan_hold and model_vae_categorical achieved 0.0 terminal shortfall yet suffered single-step late suffix blips (step 240 recon_mse=1.3706 on ae_gan_hold after hold=0.0006 at step 230; step 1100 mass_tv=0.1807 on model_vae_categorical). Root-cause inspection proved that unconditionally setting target_c = cf[win_idx] from exact single-batch integer quotas causes ordinary binomial minibatch fluctuations (e.g. 36/28 draws on a converged 50/50 model) to assign Gaussian rim samples (d_near > 1.65 * r_k, g_valley > 0) across the valley to the opposite mode even when g_rebal == 0, disrupting encoder slot correspondence. Routing valley/rim stragglers strictly to their own nearest chart cf[near_idx] unless a >2.8 SE persistent cross-chart deficit/surplus is active under thermal disequilibrium (s_thermal > 0.02, with t1c_halo_mult=2.15 capped at 0.35 * d_nn_chart) eliminates cross-valley slot-swap false alarms while preserving hard cross-mode rebalancing on genuinely collapsed modes.",
  "parent": "t1-coupling-v2",
